// Title: Python Reverse Shell Execution Via PTY And Socket Modules
// Sigma ID: 32e62bc7-3de0-4bb1-90af-532978fe42c0
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: @d4ns4n_, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-04-24 | Modified: 2024-11-04
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects the execution of python with calls to the socket and pty module in order to connect and
//   spawn a potential reverse shell.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.revshells.com/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_python_reverse_shell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath contains "python" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -c " and ProcessCommandLine contains "import" and ProcessCommandLine contains "pty" and ProcessCommandLine contains "socket" and ProcessCommandLine contains "spawn" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".connect")
